    "Home >",
    "News >",
    "USTA National Campus Pro Tennis Classic - Jan. 17 Results",
    "On Wednesday, first-round singles and doubles action continued at the USTA National Campus Pro Tennis Classic.",
    "Six Americans were among the singles winners today including former Top 100 player and 2011 junior US Open champion Grace Min, qualifier and 2017 NCAA doubles champion for Ohio State Francesca Di Lorenzo, qualifier and former University of Tennessee standout Caitlin Whoriskey, andMaria Sanchez, who played at USC. No. 1 seed Anhelina Kalinina, of Ukraine, No. 2 seedIrina Maria Bara, of Romania, and No. 4 seed Ulrikke Eikeri, of Norway, also all advanced, while two seeds were upset.",
    "Key match-ups for Thursday include Kalinina against former world No. 1 junior and 2017 junior Wimbledon champion Claire Liu, as well as Whoriskey versus Di Lorenzo in a match-up of former college stars.",
    "This is the first pro tennis event to be held at the USTA National Campus this year and one of two events scheduled at the campus in 2018, as another USTA Pro Circuit women's event will take place in March.",
    "Please note that Veteran’s Appreciation Night will be held on Friday, Jan. 19 prior to the match; Net Generation Kids' Day will be held on Saturday, Jan. 20, at 10 a.m.; and a Net Generation Team Challenge will be held on Sunday, Jan. 21, at 10 a.m. prior to the final.",
    "Players will be available for media following their matches. Please contact Amanda Korba or Dan Pyser for any staff interviews and feel free to reach out with any additional questions or requests.",
    "WEDNESDAY, JANUARY 17 – RESULTS",
    "Singles Main Draw – First Round",
    "(1) Anhelina Kalinina (UKR) def. Katherine Sebov (CAN) 6-2, 6-2",
    "(2) Irina Maria Bara (ROU) def. Victoria Rodriguez (MEX) 6-3, 6-3",
    "(4) Ulrikke Eikeri (NOR) def. (Q) Alisa Kleybanova (RUS) 7-5, 6-3",
    "Maria Sanchez (USA) def. (7) Olga Ianchuk (UKR) 6-3, 7-5",
    "(Q) Francesca Di Lorenzo (USA) def. (8) Elena Gabriela Ruse (ROU) 4-6, 7-6(3), 1-0, ret.",
    "Grace Min (USA) def. (WC) Maria Mateas (USA) 6-3, 4-6, 6-3",
    "Chiara Scholl (USA) def. (Q) Polina Leykina (RUS) 7-5, 3-6, 6-0",
    "(Q) Caitlin Whoriskey (USA) def. Usue Maitane Arconada (USA) 3-6, 6-2, 6-3",
    "(LL) Jessica Pegula (USA) def. (Q) Olga Danilovic (SRB) 6-1, 6-3",
    "Chihiro Maramatsu (JPN) def. (Q) Reka-Luca Jani (HUN) 6-2, 6-1",
    "(Q) Kyoka Okamura (JPN) def. Cristiana Ferrando (ITA) 6-2, 7-5",
    "Julia Grabher (AUT) def. (Q) Aymet Uzcategui (VEN) 6-1, 6-1",
    "Doubles Main Draw – First Round",
    "(2) Irina Maria Bara (ROU) / Maria-Teresa Torro-Flor (ESP) def. (WC) Emerald Able (USA) / Alycia Parks (USA) 6-2, 6-1",
    "(Q) Francesca Di Lorenzo (USA) / Ann Li (USA) def. (3) Sanaz Marand (USA) / Paula Cristina Goncalves (BRA) 6-3, 6-4",
    "Reka-Luca Jani (HUN) / Marcela Zacarias (MEX) def. (Q) Dasha Ivanova (USA) / Ayla Aksu (TUR) 6-0, 6-2",
    "Katharina Gerlach (GER) / Julia Wachaczyk (GER) def. Kyoka Okamura (JPN) / Ayano Shimizu (JPN) 6-4, 3-6, [10-6]",
    "ABOUT THE USTA PRO CIRCUIT With more than 90 tournaments hosted annually throughout the country and prize money ranging from $15,000 to $125,000, the USTA Pro Circuit is the pathway to the US Open and tour-level competition for aspiring tennis players and a frequent battleground for established professionals. The USTA launched its Pro Circuit 39 years ago to provide players with the opportunity to gain professional ranking points, and it has since grown to become the largest developmental tennis circuit in the world, offering more than $3 million in prize money. Last year, more than 1,000 men and women from more than 70 countries competed in cities nationwide. Andy Murray, Maria Sharapova, John Isner, Sloane Stephens, Kei Nishikori, Victoria Azarenka, and Sam Querrey and are among today’s top stars who began their careers on the USTA Pro Circuit. Follow the USTA Pro Circuit at #USTAProCircuit and www.procircuit.usta.com.",
    "Monday - Friday 7:00 AM - 9:00 PM",
